a52sxq: qtee_shmbridge: 4 MiB default pool as on 5.4

The shared QTEE shm-bridge pool is static (QCOM_TZMEM_POLICY_STATIC, never grows) and 6.12
creates it with 512 KiB; the 5.4 default bridge was 4 MiB (DEFAULT_BRIDGE_SIZE SZ_4M). Every
smcinvoke call allocates its in/out buffers from it, and the smcinvoke release path has no
fallback when the allocation fails (the TZ object is then leaked in QTEE). qseecom, ICE and
qcom_scm share the same pool. Restore the 5.4 headroom (audit 2026-11-18, low 32).

--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qtee_shmbridge.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qtee_shmbridge.c
@@ -275,7 +275,12 @@
 	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_QCOM_TZMEM_LOW_MEMORY))
 		pool_config.initial_size = SZ_256K - SZ_32K; /* 224K */
 	else
-		pool_config.initial_size = SZ_512K;
+		/*
+		 * a52sxq: 4 MiB as the 5.4 default bridge (DEFAULT_BRIDGE_SIZE), not 512 KiB. The
+		 * pool is static and shared by smcinvoke (every invoke's in/out buffers and the
+		 * object release path, which has no fallback), qseecom, ICE and qcom_scm.
+		 */
+		pool_config.initial_size = SZ_4M;
 	pool_config.policy = QCOM_TZMEM_POLICY_STATIC;
 	pool_config.max_size = pool_config.initial_size;
 	pool_config.is_cached = true;
